---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import ServiceCard from '../components/ServiceCard.astro'
---

<Page
  title="Alpisto"
  description="Engineering consulting for R&D teams. MATLAB→Python migration, power-systems algorithms, embedded BLE firmware, IoT backends. By an engineer with 20+ years across power systems, embedded, and ML."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 leading-tight mb-6">
        Engineering consulting<br class="hidden sm:block" /> for R&D teams
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        We help scientific and engineering teams move from legacy code to modern stacks —
        Python, embedded firmware, event-driven backends. By an engineer with 20+ years
        across power systems, embedded hardware, and scientific software.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="#services"
          class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors"
        >
          See services
        </a>
        <a
          href="/about"
          class="inline-block border border-slate-300 text-slate-700 font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:border-slate-900 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors"
        >
          About us
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services -->
  <section id="services" class="py-16 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">What we do</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8">
        Project-based engagements. We work hands-on — you get working code, not slide decks.
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        <ServiceCard
          title="MATLAB → Python migration"
          description="Any math, any domain. Audit, risk matrix, pilot module, full migration. From science to production-grade Python with proper testing and CI."
          href="/matlab-to-python"
        />
        <ServiceCard
          title="Power-systems algorithms"
          description="State estimation, OPF, transient stability, short-circuit analysis. Custom development in Python with pandapower, PowerFactory API, and proprietary solvers."
          href="/power-systems-algos"
          available={false}
        />
        <ServiceCard
          title="Embedded BLE devices"
          description="ESP32, nRF52, Zephyr RTOS. From prototype to production-ready firmware. We build our own FlyBeeper paragliding devices — we know this stack in production."
          href="/embedded"
          available={false}
        />
        <ServiceCard
          title="Backends for IoT/BLE fleets"
          description="FastAPI, NATS, MQTT, event-driven architecture. For hardware teams that need a reliable, scalable cloud side without hiring a full backend team."
          href="/embedded-backend"
          available={false}
        />
        <ServiceCard
          title="R&D advisory"
          description="Algorithm prototyping, technical due diligence, scientific Python coaching. Short paid engagements that prove fit before scaling. No PowerPoint consulting."
          href="/advisory"
          available={false}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who we are teaser -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Who we are</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Alpisto is a small engineering practice based in Slovenia. We focus on the technical
          problems that sit between research code and production systems — the gap where
          scientific computing meets real-world constraints.
        </p>
        <p>
          We work hands-on. Every engagement is led by a senior engineer, not delegated to
          juniors. Our own product, <a href="https://market.flybeeper.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FlyBeeper</a> — a line of BLE variometers for paragliding —
          is proof that we ship hardware, firmware, and backends together in production.
        </p>
        <p>
          We prefer short, well-scoped engagements that prove fit before scaling. If the
          problem is interesting and the timeline is realistic, we want to hear about it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/about" class="inline-block mt-6 text-blue-600 font-medium hover:underline">
        More about us →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-slate-900 text-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Have a project?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8">
        Tell us what you're building. We'll tell you honestly if we can help.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="mailto:info@alpisto.eu"
          class="inline-block bg-white text-slate-900 font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors"
        >
          info@alpisto.eu
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/evgenyistomin"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-block border border-slate-600 text-slate-300 font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:border-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors"
        >
          LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
